            {
                "entry_id": "b70ff475-d0c1-318d-8d02-3c45eca18a64",
                "word": "IBM",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7f23cf02-7028-4d7c-bd02-0af47a28faeb",
                        "entry_id": "b70ff475-d0c1-318d-8d02-3c45eca18a64",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "IBMs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "93f431c5-e216-3ae8-87a2-a95ebe14f2b1",
                        "entry_id": "b70ff475-d0c1-318d-8d02-3c45eca18a64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of intercontinental ballistic missile."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "countable",
                            "initialism",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "65d1f017-012c-4501-90f2-c0e3896d0b56",
                                "sense_id": "93f431c5-e216-3ae8-87a2-a95ebe14f2b1",
                                "text": "They see this last possibility in an international agreement to stop further atomic and thermonuclear bomb tests and halt the development of intercontinental ballistic missiles (IBMs)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc65812f-06a9-475e-9f54-094ae1de58a4",
                                "sense_id": "93f431c5-e216-3ae8-87a2-a95ebe14f2b1",
                                "text": "Today we need a defense against IBM attack. When as chief of R&D I urged Army Ordnance to develop an antimissile missile, I heard repeatedly that you can't hit a bullet with a bullet, so it is impossible to develop such a missile."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f10eaea1-b887-4f50-a326-a6366f473ade",
                                "sense_id": "93f431c5-e216-3ae8-87a2-a95ebe14f2b1",
                                "text": "Thus, they limit to a strictly defined number the quantity of armed IBMs in the USSR and the United States, as well as ballistic missiles of submarines."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba15e1d7-835d-3583-a23d-7ccd6e2e15c5",
                        "entry_id": "b70ff475-d0c1-318d-8d02-3c45eca18a64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of inclusion body myositis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "countable",
                            "initialism",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "74567be2-c119-3bbc-9348-dad4dc34f37a",
                        "entry_id": "b70ff475-d0c1-318d-8d02-3c45eca18a64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A company that dominates its field."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "figuratively",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2aa24571-0d7f-4058-9ad5-8b727f18b4d5",
                                "sense_id": "74567be2-c119-3bbc-9348-dad4dc34f37a",
                                "text": "Univac was the IBM of the computer industry's incipiency; in 1952 Univac had virtually 100% of the market."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43aadc5d-6f0e-4f53-85bc-cda0a7c12eda",
                                "sense_id": "74567be2-c119-3bbc-9348-dad4dc34f37a",
                                "text": "First, to Sperry Univac, the descendent^([sic]) of the first real computer company, which might have become the IBM of the industry had it not blown its early lead;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e1079bf-06d0-4774-a77b-91b582041602",
                                "sense_id": "74567be2-c119-3bbc-9348-dad4dc34f37a",
                                "text": "The US lead was mainly due to one firm, the IBM of its small, specialized field: Cray Research Inc."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
